    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;The room is waiting. It has always been waiting. But something is changing.&quot;</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You open the door, step through\u2014and find yourself back in the same room... Familiar, yet wrong in a way you can\u2019t quite place. There\u2019s a door behind you and a door ahead. Moving forward seems simple enough. Until it isn\u2019t.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every time you step through, the room reshapes itself, subtly\u2026 or not so subtly. A chair that wasn\u2019t there before. A shadow that lingers a little too long. A feeling, creeping at the edges of your mind\u2014that you\u2019re being watched. But by what? Or by whom?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The rules are simple:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the room is the same as when you first saw it, turn back.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If something has changed, move forward.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Count each right choice till the end.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no monsters. No chases. No jump scares. Just the growing weight of the unknown. The deeper you stare into the shifting reality, the stronger the feeling becomes\u2014<strong>something is staring back.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you reach the end? Or will the room consume you first?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>An eerie, slow-burning psychological horror where the only enemy is doubt.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3537700/extras/cf139c8f262d21cd45aa62444507224c.avif?t=1742549690\" width=800 height=320 /></span></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>&quot;The room is waiting. It has always been waiting. But something is changing.&quot;</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You open the door, step through\u2014and find yourself back in the same room... Familiar, yet wrong in a way you can\u2019t quite place. There\u2019s a door behind you and a door ahead. Moving forward seems simple enough. Until it isn\u2019t.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every time you step through, the room reshapes itself, subtly\u2026 or not so subtly. A chair that wasn\u2019t there before. A shadow that lingers a little too long. A feeling, creeping at the edges of your mind\u2014that you\u2019re being watched. But by what? Or by whom?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The rules are simple:</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If the room is the same as when you first saw it, turn back.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If something has changed, move forward.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Count each right choice till the end.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no monsters. No chases. No jump scares. Just the growing weight of the unknown. The deeper you stare into the shifting reality, the stronger the feeling becomes\u2014<strong>something is staring back.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you reach the end? Or will the room consume you first?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>An eerie, slow-burning psychological horror where the only enemy is doubt.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3537700/extras/cf139c8f262d21cd45aa62444507224c.avif?t=1742549690\" width=800 height=320 /></span></p>",
